# Copyright (c) d-SEAMS developers
# Build every VMD molfile plugin that chemfiles 0.10.4 lists as "not yet
# enabled but that should compile without issue" and whose reader returns
# atoms, and register each reader as a chemfiles format. With the three
# default plugins (gromacs, molden, psf) that is 30 plugins and 33 molfile
# formats. Left out: cifplugin (no source in molfiles.tar.gz), crdplugin and
# vtfplugin's vcf reader (no atom count without a separate topology),
# babelplugin (runs an external babel), basissetplugin (no atoms), and the
# graphics and volumetric plugins, which Molfile<F> cannot read atoms from.
# Every plugin source still ships in molfiles.tar.gz.
#
# Molfile<F> also changes for the new plugins: nsteps() counts into scratch
# buffers instead of a null timestep (rst7 crashed on a valid file), an
# empty file is an error before a plugin sees it (rst7 crashed on one),
# and a plugin that reports no atoms is an error instead of a std::vector
# length error.
